{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_comp_no_naive_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_comp_no_naive_chain","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QDifferenceOperator.lean#L81-L88","doc":"**No naive q-chain rule for a non-monomial inner function.** Concrete counterexample\nover `ℚ`: with `f = g = (·²)` (so `f ∘ g = (·⁴)`), `Δ₂((·²)∘(·²))(1) = 15`, but the naive\n\"product of q-derivatives\" `Δ₂(·²)(1²)·Δ₂(·²)(1) = 3·3 = 9`. `15 ≠ 9` — implicit\nq-differentiation through a non-monomial branch does not close. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_comp_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_comp_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QDifferenceOperator.lean#L75-L79","doc":"**The monomial q-chain rule** — the *only* surviving composition rule, with `q`\nrescaled to `q^m`: `Δ_q(f ∘ (·^m))(x) = Δ_{q^m}(f)(x^m)`, because `(q·x)^m = q^m·x^m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_pow","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QDifferenceOperator.lean#L69-L73","doc":"**Monomial action.** `Δ_q(·^n)(x) = (q^n − 1)·x^n`. (Divide by `(q−1)x` to recover\n`D_q(x^n) = [n]_q·x^{n−1}`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_mul","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QDifferenceOperator.lean#L61-L67","doc":"**q-Leibniz (product) rule** — the clean one:\n`Δ_q(f·g)(x) = Δ_q(f)(x)·g(x) + f(q·x)·Δ_q(g)(x)`. This is the structural reason\nq-difference *modules* are well-behaved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_const_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_const_mul","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QDifferenceOperator.lean#L56-L59","doc":"**Constant scaling.** `Δ_q(c • f) = c • Δ_q f` (as `c * f` pointwise). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_add","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QDifferenceOperator.lean#L51-L54","doc":"**Additivity.** `Δ_q(f + g) = Δ_q f + Δ_q g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff_apply","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QDifferenceOperator.lean#L48-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qDiff","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QDifferenceOperator.lean#L41-L44","doc":"**The q-difference operator** (numerator form) `Δ_q f = x ↦ f(q·x) − f(x)`.\nEquals `(q−1)·x · D_q f(x)` for the Jackson derivative `D_q`; division-free, so total\nover any `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator.qShift","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QDifferenceOperator.lean#L38-L39","doc":"**The q-shift** `σ_q f = x ↦ f(q·x)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}